    <bpmn:process id="W_W4378" name="W4378. Root-Cause Service Failure Analysis &amp; Remediation Plan" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Repeat/critical/systemic finding; pattern detected
Frequency: Per pattern + periodic
Volume: Systemic/pattern service-failure analyses
Owner: Service Quality / OpEx (VS-133) / CX (VS-13)
Participants: Service Quality, OpEx (VS-133), CX (VS-13), Store Ops (VS-07), HR (VS-103), Strategy (VS-33)
Source: workflow W4378 — Root-Cause Service Failure Analysis &amp; Remediation Plan</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4378_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4378_Lane1" name="Service Quality">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4378_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4378_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4378_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4378_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4378_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4378_Start3" name="Repeat/critical/systemic finding; pattern detected">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4378_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4378_Task4" name="Service Quality/OpEx identify patterns &amp; systemic failures (repeated across…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Service Quality/OpEx identify patterns &amp; systemic failures (repeated across stores/regions/associates), and run root-cause analysis (5-why, process VS-133)
Responsible (R): Service Quality / OpEx
Accountable (A): Head of Service Quality / OpEx Lead
Duration: Per pattern</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4378_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4378_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4378_Task5" name="Cross-functional team design the remediation plan (training VS-124, process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cross-functional team design the remediation plan (training VS-124, process redesign VS-133, staffing VS-19.3, tools, policy) addressing root cause
Responsible (R): Service Quality / OpEx / Store Ops / HR
Accountable (A): COO / CHRO
Duration: Per pattern</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4378_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4378_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4378_Task6" name="Service Quality/OpEx track remediation impact on subsequent service scores, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Service Quality/OpEx track remediation impact on subsequent service scores, and standardize/scale successful fixes
Responsible (R): Service Quality / OpEx
Accountable (A): Head of Service Quality / OpEx Lead
Duration: Periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4378_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4378_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4378_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4378_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4378_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-670 (ensure controlled execution — Findings Remediation, Recognition &amp; Service-Quality Analytics (PA-146.3).) | - CTL-670: systemic failures root-caused (VS-133); remediation addresses root cause; impact tracked &amp; scaled
Owner: Service Quality / OpEx (VS-133) / CX (VS-13)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4378_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4378_Annotation8" targetRef="W4378_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
